      {
        "id": 57558,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-03T21:46:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"j1hopki1\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> j1hopki1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But, wait. Where's the Final Wasteland card? <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/frowning.png?v=12\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>There are only so many cards in an environment deck. There are 12 existing decks &nbsp;and probably at least six more planned (2 each in Vengeance and in each of the 5th and 6th expansions). There was never going to be room for all of the environments. My guess is that The Typhoon displaced something and when something had to give they took it from The Final Wasteland because that was a stretch goal which might not have been reached.</p>",
